{"id": 75, "ts": 1780615495.173084, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s reminder that we have no concrete evidence of Candidate\u202fD\u2019s ability to manage the complex avionics and systems required for long\u2011distance international flights. That gap, combined with the reported arrogance, hot temper, and weak leadership, raises serious doubts about his crew\u2011cooperation and professional communication\u2014both non\u2011negotiable for safety\u2011critical cockpit work.\nCandidate\u202fB, on the other hand, has clear strengths that map directly to our key criteria: he is very conscientious, handles stress well, and demonstrates solid technical aptitude through excellent weather\u2011assessment skills and strong computer proficiency. While his grumpiness and occasional uncooperativeness are concerns, they appear less severe than D\u2019s documented attitude issues and can be mitigated with coaching and clear behavioral expectations.\nGiven the lack of technical competence evidence for D and the higher risk to crew dynamics, I shift my provisional vote to **Candidate\u202fB** as the better overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
